+FCS_RBG_EXT.1 specifies deterministic random bit generation in accordance with ISO/IEC 18031:2011 using an identified DRBG mechanism, and requires the deterministic RBG to be seeded by at least one entropy source that provides a minimum amount of entropy at least equal to the greatest security strength of the keys and hashes that the RBG will generate. The cryptographic SFRs in this cPP that require random bits rely on FCS_RBG_EXT.1 for both the deterministic random bit generation mechanism and the entropy-source seeding requirement.
