+Common Criteria Part 2 includes a random bit generation component, FCS_RBG.1. FCS_RBG.1 carries a defined dependency structure, including dependencies on FCS_RBG.2 or FCS_RBG.3 for external or internal seeding, and dependencies on FPT_FLS.1, Failure with preservation of secure state, and FPT_TST.1, TSF self-testing. Use of FCS_RBG.1 would therefore require the cPP to include or justify additional dependent requirements that are broader than the random bit generation baseline established for conformant TOEs.
+
+The intended cPP baseline is limited to the deterministic random bit generation mechanism, the applicable standard, and the entropy-source seeding requirement. FCS_RBG_EXT.1 states this baseline precisely as a single, self-contained component, without adding broader failure-state or TSF self-testing requirements that are not part of this random bit generation baseline. It is also referenced consistently by the cryptographic SFRs in this cPP that require random bits.
+
+FCS_RBG_EXT.1 is therefore retained and placed in the FCS class.
